id: pm-fr10t8
title: "A continuable key=value prose segment containing a colon is misread as a new key, so --comment/--note/--learning seeds store the raw entry with its text= prefix"
description: "The shared key=value grammar (parseCsvKv in src/core/item/parse.ts) splits a continuable prose value on commas and then treats any later segment containing a colon or equals sign as a NEW key, even when the candidate key is not an identifier. For --comment, --note and --learning seeds, parseLogSeed then sees an \"unsupported key\" and falls back to storing the whole raw entry, so the immutable comment keeps the literal text= prefix the agent wrote as syntax.\n\nReproduced on pm 2026.11.1 in a sandbox: pm create --title t --type Task --comment \"text=(a, b) c. Related: d\" stores \"text=(a, b) c. Related: d\". The segment \" b) c. Related: d\" is parsed as key \"b) c. Related\" with value \"d\". \"text=a. Related: b\" (no comma) and \"text=a (b, c); d\" (no colon after the comma) both round-trip correctly, which is why the defect only shows up in longer prose. Observed in practice on pm-gh1647: its create-time intake comment is stored with a text= prefix.\n\npm-hu92i3 fixed the three comma behaviours (whitespace, escapes, quotes) but not this delimiter-in-continuation case. The markdown-line parser already requires keys to match [A-Za-z0-9_.-]+; the CSV path does not."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,annotations,cli,data-integrity,parsing
created_at: "2026-11-01T10:57:52.974Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T15:40:56.290Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-01T12:21:43.403Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-01T12:21:43.403Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "parseCsvKv treats a segment whose candidate key is not an identifier ([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+) as a continuation of the active continuable key instead of a new key; pm create --comment/--note/--learning with text=(a, b) c. Related: d stores exactly (a, b) c. Related: d; GH-258 strict unknown-key rejection still refuses an identifier-shaped typo key such as lable=main; a seed with an identifier-shaped unknown key (for example source=dogfood) keeps the lossless raw-entry fallback"
parent: pm-yql1
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "parseCsvKv treats a post-comma segment as a continuation of the active continuable value when its candidate key is non-empty and not identifier-shaped ([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+); empty keys still refuse, typo keys still open keys for strict unknown-key rejection, and identifier-keyed seeds keep the lossless raw-entry fallback. Rule documented in docs/AGENT_EVIDENCE_CONSISTENCY.md."
expected_result: "text=(a, b) c. Related: d is recorded as (a, b) c. Related: d."
actual_result: "parse-utils and context-integrity-recovery specs pass, including continuation, typo, empty-key and identifier-keyed raw fallback cases; create-command lossless-seed spec still passes."
